   "source": [
    "## Cell 9: What you just ran (the elevator pitch)\n",
    "\n",
    "**The full stack, end-to-end, in one Colab run:**\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **DetectionPipeline** — YOLO26 with NMS-free architecture, ONNX export for CPU/GPU portability\n",
    "2. **TrackingPipeline** — ByteTrack multi-object tracker with stable IDs across frames\n",
    "3. **DriftMonitor** — 3-signal drift detection (KS test on confidence, z-score on counts, MAD on latency)\n",
    "4. **L1TriageAgent** — 7 deterministic severity rules (drift, low confidence, stuck track, hazardous class, large bbox)\n",
    "5. **MaintenanceAdvisor** — turns drift signals into actionable maintenance hints (severity + action + why)\n",
    "6. **MonitoringDashboard** — per-shift report with retrain recommendation\n",
    "7. **RobustnessTestSuite** — 13 MRF-condition augmentations, broken/degraded/ok classification\n",
    "8. **MCPTriageSurface** — the 5-tool MCP server for the L1 ROC agent (programmatic; not started in this notebook)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Test coverage:** 171 unit tests, all passing (1 skipped — rclpy not on Colab). 4 framework abstractions + 7 JD modules + bonus triage agent. Model-agnostic (swap to YOLO27s in one line). Production patterns (thread-safe, error-resilient, import-safe).

